WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome back.
We're hanging out with

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.100
the one and only Nicole Kidman!

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.100
Oh, my goodness.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:08.100
You're playing Lucille Ball

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.434
in this new movie.
-Yes.

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:12.267
-Now, this is --
How do you go about this?

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:14.767
It is an impression?
No.

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.267
You can't do an impression.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:19.934
-I mean, when Aaron originally
approached me, he was like,

00:00:19.934 --> 00:00:22.934
"I do not want you to do an
impersonation of her,"

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:26.267
which, thank God,
because I can't.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:27.767
I wouldn't be able to.

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:31.267
So, he said, "I really
want to discov--"

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:35.100
I mean, it's about this marriage
and Desi and Lucille.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.801
And I call her Lucille
so that you really can

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:41.300
sort of understand that it's not
the "I Love Lucy" show.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.300
-Yeah, there are two --
the way you did it,

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.534
like, "I Love Lucy"
is one character

00:00:45.534 --> 00:00:47.033
and then Lucille Ball is --

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:48.701
-Yeah, and Lucille Ball
always said

00:00:48.701 --> 00:00:51.033
she as a woman was not funny.

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:53.367
And you would be able
to attest to this --

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:54.868
comedy is hard.

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:56.701
[ Laughter ]
-Oh!

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:58.367
I thought you were gonna say...

00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:00.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:01.934
-What did you think?
-I don't care.

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:03.434
I mean -- I mean --

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:05.601
Yes, comedy is definitely hard.
Yeah.

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:07.267
-Very hard.
-Yes.

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.100
-But --
-And it ain't funny right now.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.434
-Oh!
What are you talking about?!

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:11.701
-Oh, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:13.334
-But she was one of the best
physical comedians.

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:16.000
-Yeah, and I mean,
for me as an actor,

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.667
and primarily a dramatic actor,
I was like, "Oh, my God.

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:20.000
How do you do this?" and...

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.334
-You nailed it.
-When I started to study her,

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:25.334
I was like, "oh, I love
playing this woman,"

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:28.834
because the physical comedy
and the movement of the body

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:31.667
and being able to release
into that as an actor

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:33.000
is something I've never done.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.834
-What you did on it
that was fantastic

00:01:34.834 --> 00:01:36.934
is that you do Lucy
when the show is on

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:39.100
and your voice is higher,
and you -- "Ricky!"

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.601
and you're doing this whole --
-Waaaah!

00:01:40.601 --> 00:01:42.601
-Yes. Oh, my God.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:43.834
That is that.

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:45.300
Waaah!
And that's what she does.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.300
-Waaah! Waaah!
-And in real life -- yeah.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.467
And in real life when she talks,
she's a smoker --

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:51.300
smoked a lot.
-She had a very deep voice.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.801
She was a heavy smoker.
-Yeah.

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:54.467
I say it when you're not here,

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:55.901
but I'll say it
when you're here --

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:58.234
you're one of the best actors
that ever lived; I love you.

00:01:58.234 --> 00:01:59.400
-No.
-Yes, you're amazing.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:02.467
Everything you're in,
I absolutely buy it.

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:06.067
Hook, line, and sinker, I'm in.
I always go -- You are amazing

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:08.133
in every single thing.
-I love it. I love acting.

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:11.467
I'm very privileged to be able
to do what I love doing.

00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:13.300
-You're fantastic.
And please keep doing it.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.133
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Nicole Kidman

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:17.133
as Lucille Ball
in "Being the Ricardos."

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:18.334
Take a look.

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:19.501
-Act one, interior,

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:20.968
the Ricardos' living room,
night.

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:23.968
-Excuse me. Donald.
-Y-Yes.

00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:25.601
-Good morning. I'm Lucille Ball.

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:28.067
-I sure know that, Lucy.
-I wanted to make sure

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:29.501
because you haven't been here
in a while.

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:31.667
Is it because you've been going
through puberty?

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:34.467
-I look young, yes, but I went
through it a long time ago.

00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:35.634
And I haven't been here because

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:37.467
I've been directing
at "Danny Thomas."

00:02:37.467 --> 00:02:39.634
-With the Communist kid?
[Bleep] off.

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:41.601
-Jesus Christ.
-You don't have to [bleep] off,

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:44.100
but you do need to know
that Danny does jokes --

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.601
few people do it better --
I do physical comedy.

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:48.100
-I've seen every episode
of the show.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.601
-So have 60 million
other people.

00:02:50.601 --> 00:02:53.100
Are none of them professional
television directors?

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.767
-She's kidding.
-I can tell.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:56.267
-I'm hazing you a little,
Donald.

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:57.601
It's just my way of saying

00:02:57.601 --> 00:02:59.767
I have no confidence
in you at all.

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:02.501
-That's it.
Nicole Kidman, everybody.

00:03:02.501 --> 00:03:05.400
"Being the Ricardos"
is in theaters December 10th

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:08.234
and available on Prime Video
December 21st.

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:09.801
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

